/*!
    \page vscodeext-how-to-cpp.html
    \previouspage vscodeext-tutorials.html
    \nextpage vscodeext-reference.html

    \title Develop Qt applications

    With the Qt C++ extension pack, you can:

    \list
        \li Create Qt applications with Qt Widgets based UIs
        \li Use Qt in your CMake project by selecting a generated Qt kit
        \li Get syntax highlighting and code completion for Qt-specific
            file formats
        \li Design Qt widgets-based UIs with \l{\QD}
        \li Build Qt projects with \l{Build with CMake}{CMake}
        \li Debug Qt's C++ types
        \li Read \l {Qt Documentation}
    \endlist

    \section1 How to develop Qt applications

    \generatelist vscodeext-how-to-cpp
*/

/*!
    \page vscodeext-how-to-qtquick.html
    \previouspage vscodeext-how-to-cpp.html
    \nextpage vscodeext-how-to-python.html

    \title Develop Qt Quick applications

    With the Qt QML extension, you can:

    \list
        \li Create Qt Quick applications
        \li Get QML syntax highlighting and code completion with
            \l {\QMLLS}
        \li Verify the syntax of QML code with \l{qmllint Reference}{qmllint}
        \li Find causes for typical performance problems in Qt Quick applications
            with QML Profiler
    \endlist

    \section1 How to develop Qt Quick applications

    \generatelist vscodeext-how-to-qml
*/

/*!
    \page vscodeext-how-to-csharp.html
    \previouspage vscodeext-how-to-qtquick.html
    \nextpage vscodeext-how-to-python.html

    \title Develop with C#

    With the Qt C# extension pack, you can develop C# applications with
    VS Code and \l {Qt Bridge for C#}:

    \list
        \li Create C# applications with Qt Quick based UIs
        \li Build, run, and debug Qt projects with .NET
        \li Get QML syntax highlighting and code completion with
            \l {\QMLLS}
        \li Live preview QML applications
    \endlist
*/

/*!
    \page vscodeext-how-to-python.html
    \previouspage vscodeext-how-to-csharp.html
    \nextpage vscodeext-how-to-web.html

    \title Develop with Python

    With the Qt Python extension pack, you can develop \l {Qt for Python}
    applications with VS Code and Python:

    \list
        \li Install PySide6 packages
        \li Create Qt for Python applications with Qt Quick or Qt Widgets based UIs
        \li Build, run, and clean the applications
        \li Debug the applications with \c debugpy and QML debugger
        \li Read Qt for Python documentation
    \endlist

    \section1 How to develop with Python

    \generatelist vscodeext-how-to-python
*/

/*!
    \page vscodeext-how-to-web.html
    \previouspage vscodeext-how-to-python.html
    \nextpage vscodeext-reference.html

    \title Develop for the web

    With the \l {Qt for WebAssembly} extension pack, you can:

    \list
        \li Use Qt in your CMake project by selecting a generated Qt kit
        \li Get syntax highlighting and code completion for Qt-specific
            file formats
        \li Build Qt projects with CMake
        \li Debug Qt for WebAssembly code
        \li Read Qt documentation
    \endlist

    \section1 How to develop for WebAssembly

    \generatelist vscodeext-how-to-wasm
*/
